From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James M Snell <jasnell@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Jun 2023 15:29:26 -0700
Subject: Implement Promise Context Tagging

Every promise records the isolate's current promise context tag, the
PromiseContextTag root, which Isolate::PromiseContextScope sets.
Outside any scope the tag is the hole. Following a pending promise
whose tag is neither the hole nor the current tag calls the
embedder's PromiseCrossContextCallback, which may return another
promise to follow instead. Builtins copy and compare the tag inline,
and call the runtime only when the tags differ.

Optimized code allocates promises inline while the PromiseHook
protector holds, without tagging them, so setting the callback
invalidates the protector. PromiseContextTagTest checks the promises
that Maglev and TurboFan would otherwise allocate inline.

Signed-off-by: James M Snell <jsnell@cloudflare.com>

